# `golem` (runtime)

**Game loop + integrated networking + world data + interest management:** `Server`, `ServerConfig` (with `Addr`, `Path`, `StaticDir`, `Transport`, `StateUpdateLane`, `CellSize` for FOI, optional `LogReplicationStats` (or env `GOLEM_LOG_REPLICATION_STATS=1`) for once-per-second replication batching / wire-size diagnostics), `TickFunc` `func(dt float64, s *Server)`, `ContactFunc` `func(contacts []CollisionContact)`, `OnTick` / `OnUpdates` / `OnContact`, `SetRemovalSerializer`, `SetCollisionBackend`, `Run` with fixed timestep. **Entity world API on `Server`:** `CreateEntity(e, owner ...int64) error` (unowned vs owned via optional session ID), `DeleteEntity`, `Get`, `Owner`, `SetOwner`, `All`, `Len`, `SnapshotAll`—all delegate to an internal `*registry.Registry` (`reg` field, unexported). Optional **`ServerBinder`** (`BindServer(*Server)`): `CreateEntity` calls it after ID assignment and before registry insertion, so `OnSpawn` can use a bound server; snapshot restore goes through `CreateEntity` and gets the same binding. CreateEntity uses `AddWithoutSpawn`/`AddOwnedWithoutSpawn` then collider registration then `registry.NotifySpawn` so spawn hooks observe bound server and registered colliders. **Session avatars:** `SpawnAvatar(sess, e, AvatarOptions{FOIRadius, FOIMargin})` does `CreateEntity(e, sess.ID)`, assigns FOI when `FOIRadius > 0` (errors if interest is disabled or radius is negative; `0` disables FOI), and records concurrency-safe `sessionID↔entityID` indexes under `avatarMu` (not held across registry hooks or interest ops). FOI goes through `AssignFOI`/`RemoveFOI` (`interestMu`). Lock order when both are needed: `interestMu` before `avatarMu`. `Avatar(sessionID)` and generic `AvatarOf[T](s, sessionID)` look up the bound entity. Duplicate `SpawnAvatar` for a live avatar is rejected (no replace). On disconnect, user `OnDisconnect` runs first (avatar still readable; listener always delivers a non-nil `*Session`), then automatic `RemoveFOI` (when interest enabled) and reaping of any avatar still bound to the session — including a replacement spawned inside the callback — so avatars cannot leak past disconnect. Mid-session `DeleteEntity` clears matching avatar indexes in O(1). `SetOwner` changes command authority only — it does not transfer avatar identity. `NewServer` always creates an internal `golem/net.Listener` wired to that registry, with `WrapEntityUpdate` as the reliable stream entity message wrapper and a world snapshot closure. Automatic incremental entity replication uses `StateUpdateLaneDatagram` over WebTransport by default; `StateUpdateLaneStream` keeps incremental updates on the reliable stream. Datagram state updates use compact state records for known-entity deltas and fall oversized/full-state payloads back to the reliable stream. When `CellSize > 0`, an `interest.Manager` is created and interest management is enabled (entity snapshots on connect are deferred). When `Addr` is set, `Run` starts both the tick loop and the built-in HTTP server plus the selected transport endpoint (WebTransport by default, WebSocket when configured with `StateUpdateLaneStream`). When `Addr` is empty, `Run` only ticks; the game mounts `Handler()` on its own router or HTTP/3 server.

**Interest management:** when enabled (`CellSize > 0`), `AssignFOI(sessionID, entityID, radius, margin)` and `RemoveFOI(sessionID)` control per-session fields of interest. All Server FOI / visibility / broadcast-known access (`AssignFOI`, `RemoveFOI`, visibility group APIs, `SessionsKnowing` known-set reads, and the `UpdateGrid`+`ComputeDiffsFiltered` critical section) is guarded by `interestMu` so gameplay can call these APIs off the tick goroutine; `interestMu` is not held across network sends or registry hooks. `runInterestTick` copies filtered diffs under the mutex, then flushes and sends unlocked. Entered entities get `FullUpdate`, stayed+dirty get delta or compact datagram record, exited get removal. Global entities (`IsGlobal() == true`) bypass distance but still honor visibility-group membership. Sessions without FOI still receive no entities (including grouped globals). When interest is **not** enabled, `runBroadcastTick` uses per-session known-set diffs when visibility groups (or known-set reconciliation) require it, and keeps blind `BroadcastBatch` as a fast path when every session already knows the live public set.

**Visibility groups:** `Server` always owns one `golem/visibility.Manager` (no policy mirroring into interest). Public APIs: `JoinVisibilityGroup`, `LeaveVisibilityGroup`, `SetEntityVisibilityGroup` (empty group = public). Concurrency-safe under `interestMu` and never wait on network I/O. Policy is point-in-time: blind-vs-filtered decisions and connect-snapshot allowed-ID selection linearize under `interestMu`, then the mutex is released before `FullUpdate` / `BroadcastBatch` / writes. A mutation after that decision takes effect on the next replication pass via known-set enter/exit (already selected/queued frames are not retroactively revoked). `SessionsKnowing` consults actual known sets in both modes, never raw membership. Broadcast known state is cleared if SendBatch observes a disconnected session after enter decisions. Group/tombstone metadata for deleted entities is retained until that tick's removal decisions are handled, then cleared. Disconnect clears session membership and broadcast known state (FOI cleanup remains in avatar disconnect).

**Collision integration:** opt-in via `SetCollisionBackend(b collision.Backend)` / `SetCollision3DBackend`. When a backend is set, each tick runs after `onTick` and before the flush: (1) `backend.Update` for every live entity, (2) `backend.Step(dt)` → contacts, (3) `backend.ReadBack` writes physics-corrected positions back to `PositionWriter` / 3D writers, (4) `onContact` / `onContact3D` when contacts were found, (5) 2D-only `dispatchContactEvents` when enabled (pre-existing; not part of schema-collider 3D parity). **Named layers:** `CollisionLayers` (2D) and `CollisionLayers3D` (3D) with `Bind`/`Define`/`SetCollides`/`Add`/`Set`/`Remove`/`Layer`/`Mask`/`MaskFor`; store via `SetCollisionLayers` / `SetCollisionLayers3D`. Generated `EnableCollision`/`EnableCollision3D` call `MustCollisionBackend`/`MustCollisionBackend3D` so nil backends panic before installing helpers. **Automatic schema colliders:** `ColliderProvider` and `ColliderProvider3D` register/unregister independently when both helpers are set; `CreateEntity` (including snapshot restore) registers after successful `AddWithoutSpawn` and before `NotifySpawn`/`OnSpawn`; `DeleteEntity` removes after avatar index cleanup and before registry deletion/`OnRemove`. Missing layer helpers skip registration without panicking; call EnableCollision helpers (or setters) before spawning/snapshot-loading collidable entities. Failed duplicate CreateEntity does not register a collider. **Spatial queries** (`spatial.go`): `OverlapBox`/`OverlapCircle`/`OverlapBox3D`/`OverlapSphere` (and cast helpers) return entity IDs from the collision backend; free function `OverlapOfType[T Entity](s, entityIDs)` resolves those IDs via `Server.Get`, retains only entities satisfying `T`, preserves input order, skips missing IDs, returns nil when input or result is empty, and always panics on nil `*Server` with `golem: OverlapOfType: Server must be non-nil` (including empty ID lists)—compose as `OverlapOfType[*Mob](s, s.OverlapCircle(...))` rather than adding geometry-specific generics.

**Per-entity collision events:** opt-in via `EnableContactEvents()`, which sets `contactEventsEnabled = true` and allocates `triggerPairs map[[2]int64]struct{}` and `solidPairs map[[2]int64]struct{}` (both fields on `Server`, defined in `loop.go`). Requires a collision backend. Six opt-in entity interfaces in `golem/collision_events.go`: `TriggerEnter`, `TriggerStay`, `TriggerExit` (method arg: `other Entity`); `CollisionEnter`, `CollisionStay`, `CollisionExit` (method args: `other Entity, normal CollisionVec2, depth float64`). `dispatchContactEvents(contacts []collision.Contact)` in `collision_events.go`: splits contacts into `currentTrigger` (Depth==0) and `currentSolid` (Depth>0) maps keyed by `contactKey(a,b int64) [2]int64` (canonical min-first pair); fires Enter/Stay/Exit by comparing current maps against `triggerPairs`/`solidPairs`; swaps the maps at the end. **Normal convention:** `Contact.Normal` is the push direction for `Contact.A` (unit vector from B toward A); entity B receives the negated vector so both sides get a normal pointing away from the other. **nil other:** if `reg.Get` returns false for a partner, `other` is passed as nil; the receiver entity still gets the callback (guarded by its own `okA`/`okB`). Both sides can be stale simultaneously — neither fires. `contactKey` returns `{min(a,b), max(a,b)}`.

Each tick order: **`s.tick++`** → **`OnTickStart(tick)`** → **`drainMessages()`** (OnConnect / OnMessage / OnDisconnect callbacks here) → **`reg.TickAll(dt)`** → `onTick(dt, s)` → collision step (Update → Step → ReadBack → onContact → dispatchContactEvents) → flush + broadcast → **`OnTickEnd(tick, wall)`**. `tick` is a `uint64` field on `Server`, incremented at the top of each tick (1-based, no atomic needed — single goroutine). `Tick() uint64` returns it for use in game logic (sequence numbers, log lines). All hook callbacks run on the tick goroutine, so `runtime/trace` regions and `pprof.Do` labels nest cleanly with work done in `OnTick`.

**Session event queue:** `OnConnect`, `OnMessage`, and `OnDisconnect` are enqueued from connection goroutines (via internal `enqueueConnect` / `enqueueMessage` / `enqueueDisconnect` hooks installed on the `Listener` in `NewServer`) and dispatched on the tick goroutine during `drainMessages`. The user-facing `OnConnect(fn)` / `OnMessage(fn)` / `OnDisconnect(fn)` methods **only store `fn`** — they no longer call `s.listener.On*`. This makes it safe to call `CreateEntity`, `DeleteEntity`, entity `Set*` methods, and all other `Server` APIs from all three callbacks without any additional synchronization. After the user `OnDisconnect` callback, the server runs avatar auto-cleanup (`RemoveFOI` / delete avatar entity / clear indexes). Events are queued in a buffered channel of capacity 4096; if the queue is full the event is dropped and a warning is logged (the connection goroutine is never blocked). Each event fires up to one tick after it occurs — `OnConnect` in particular fires on the tick after the world-state snapshot is delivered, which shifts when the player entity appears relative to the interest system's first visibility pass. `OnUpgrade` is unaffected and still runs synchronously before the WebSocket is accepted.

**External router support:** `Handler()` returns the active transport endpoint handler for mounting on a custom router (e.g. Chi alongside REST routes). `OnUpgrade(func(*http.Request) (any, error))` provides pre-upgrade auth; the returned value populates `Session.Data` before `OnConnect` fires, and a non-nil error rejects with HTTP 401. For token-in-query-param upgrades, use `golem/auth.UpgradeHandler` (stdlib-only helper; does not import `golem`). When using WebTransport on a caller-owned server, pair `Handler()` with `WebTransportServer(...)` on HTTP/3. Session lifecycle hooks: `OnConnect`, `OnMessage`, `OnDisconnect`, and `OnDatagram` for the lossy WebTransport lane. Direct-send helpers: `Send(sessionID, data)`, `Broadcast(data)`, `SendUnreliable(data)` / `BroadcastUnreliable(data)` when the transport supports datagrams.

**`servermsg.go`**: `WrapEntityUpdate` wraps `EntityUpdate` bytes in a `ServerMessage` envelope (proto field 1, length-delimited). `WrapWorldUpdate` wraps `WorldUpdate` bytes in a `ServerMessage` envelope (proto field 2, length-delimited). The `Listener` applies `WrapEntityUpdate` transparently via its `messageWrapper`; world frames bypass it entirely and use `WrapWorldUpdate` via the world snapshot closure or `BroadcastRaw`.

**`export.go`** re-exports `Entity`, opt-in entity interfaces `Ticker`, `Spawner`, `Remover`, `PositionWriter`, `Session` (from `golem/net`), `InterestManager`, `InterestFOI`, `InterestDiff` (from `golem/interest`), `WorldData`/`WorldStore` (from `golem/world`), and collision types including `CollisionBackend`, `CollisionShape`, `CollisionLayers`, `CollisionBackend3D`, `CollisionShape3D`, `CollisionLayers3D`, and related shape/contact aliases so consumers use a single **`golem`** import path. Six per-entity collision event interfaces (`TriggerEnter`, `TriggerStay`, `TriggerExit`, `CollisionEnter`, `CollisionStay`, `CollisionExit`) are defined directly in `golem/collision_events.go`. **`Registry` / `FlushResult` / `NewRegistry` are not re-exported**—use `golem.Server` for gameplay or import `golem/registry` for low-level embedding.

**World data** (`Server.World`): `*world.Store` is always initialized. `Server.PushWorldData(name) error` broadcasts one world type to all sessions; returns nil when the name is missing or networking is inactive, and returns a non-nil error if `MarshalUpdate` fails. `Server.SendWorldData(sessionID, data) error` is the primary per-session API: it marshals the supplied value directly (no `World.Set`), wraps with `WrapWorldUpdate`, and sends on the reliable stream to that session only — two sessions may receive different values with the same `WorldName`. Nil and typed-nil `data` return `golem: SendWorldData requires non-nil world data`. `Server.SendStoredWorldData(sessionID, name) error` matches `PushWorldData`'s missing-name nil/no-op, then delegates to `SendWorldData`. Marshal, oversize (32000-byte reliable frame cap), and disconnected-session errors propagate. `ServerConfig.WorldSnapshotExclude` lists names omitted from the connect snapshot; `NewServer` copies/normalizes the slice (drops empties/duplicates) into an immutable-after-construction exclude set used by the world snapshot closure. Excluded entries remain in `Server.World`; callers own on-demand delivery. Large embedded maps should use `map_url`. On connect, the listener still sends (non-excluded) world data before entity snapshots, in deterministic sorted name order.

**`golem/world`** package: `Data` interface (`WorldName`, `MarshalUpdate`), thread-safe `Store` (`Set`, `Get`, `MarshalAll` / `MarshalAllExcept(exclude)` in sorted name order). Pure data/serialization only — no session or network policy. No dependencies on `golem`, `golem/net`, or `golem/registry`.

Depends on **`golem/registry`** for entity storage, **`golem/net`** for networking, **`golem/interest`** for FOI management, **`golem/visibility`** for named group policy, **`golem/world`** for world data, and **`github.com/demiurgos-hub/golem-engine/golem/collision`** (local sibling module, resolved by `go.work`) for the collision backend interface; does **not** implement `Entity` or registry internals—those stay in `golem/registry/`.

**`golem/debug`** subpackage: `StartPprof(addr string) error` starts a pprof HTTP debug server on `addr` (e.g. `"127.0.0.1:6060"`). Uses a dedicated `http.ServeMux` — `http.DefaultServeMux` is not touched. All pprof handlers (`/debug/pprof/`, `/cmdline`, `/profile`, `/symbol`, `/trace`) are mounted explicitly via the named `net/http/pprof` import. Since the import lives only in `golem/debug`, production binaries that do not import it never register pprof handlers. Call from `main` behind a flag; never import in production builds.
